        "The same actor can trigger execution with `/startbackup`, which again only uses `current_user_can('backwpup')` in `src/Backups/API/Rest.php:81-82` and `src/Backups/API/Rest.php:94-100`. `start_backup()` calls `$this->job_adapter->get_jobrun_url( 'runnow', $jobid )` in `src/Backups/API/Rest.php:157-260`, which reaches `wp_remote_post()` to `wp-cron.php` in `inc/class-job.php:1850-1887`.",
        "When the job runs with the attacker-controlled S3 settings, `BackWPup_Destination_S3::job_run_archive()` uploads the produced archive via `putObject()` or multipart `uploadPart()` in `inc/class-destination-s3.php:511-551` and `inc/class-destination-s3.php:608-643`, and logs the resulting object URL in `inc/class-destination-s3.php:679-685`."
      ],
      "defenses": [
        "The legacy UI consistently treats edit/run actions as privileged: Jobs UI only renders edit/delete for `backwpup_jobs_edit` and run-now for `backwpup_jobs_start` in `inc/class-page-jobs.php:298-304`.",
        "The issue is therefore not intended behavior for the read-only role; the REST layer is weaker than the rest of the plugin's authorization model."
      ],
      "refutation": [
        {
          "attempt": "Check whether the shipped `backwpup_check` role already includes the narrower edit/start/settings capabilities, which would make the route checks consistent.",
          "result": "not_refuted",
          "details": "`inc/class-install.php:142-158` explicitly sets `backwpup_jobs_edit`, `backwpup_jobs_start`, and `backwpup_settings` to `false` for `backwpup_check`."
        },
        {
          "attempt": "Check whether a read-only role can realistically obtain the REST nonce and route URLs needed to invoke these endpoints.",
          "result": "not_refuted",
          "details": "The role can open BackWPup jobs/backups pages, and `enqueue_admin_assets()` plus `get_backwpup_api_data()` expose `wp_rest` nonce and the relevant write endpoints on any BackWPup screen in `inc/class-admin.php:100-129` and `inc/class-admin.php:1225-1253`."
        },
        {
          "attempt": "Check whether the storage save path is only reachable through a request shape that would not populate `$_POST`, which the destination save methods rely on.",
          "result": "not_refuted",
          "details": "The plugin's own client code sends form-encoded POST data to `cloudsaveandtest` through jQuery AJAX in `assets/js/backwpup-admin.js:826-839` and `assets/js/backwpup-admin.js:1317-1329`, matching the `$_POST` reads in `inc/class-destination-s3.php:163-243`."
        }
      ],
      "conclusion": "This is a confirmed privilege escalation inside the plugin's own role model. A user who should only inspect jobs/backups can store attacker-controlled cloud credentials, bind them to a job, and trigger a backup upload to attacker-controlled storage, disclosing the site's backup contents."
    },
    "poc_description": "Assign a test account the shipped `backwpup_check` role. Log in and open any BackWPup page to obtain `backwpupApi.nonce`. Use that nonce to POST attacker-controlled S3 parameters to `/wp-json/backwpup/v1/cloudsaveandtest`, then enable S3 for an existing job via `/wp-json/backwpup/v1/updatejob` or `/wp-json/backwpup/v2/storages`, and finally POST `/wp-json/backwpup/v1/startbackup` for that job. The generated archive is uploaded to the attacker-controlled S3 bucket.",
    "cvss_vector": "AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:L/A:L",
    "remediation": "Do not gate write routes with the broad `backwpup` capability. Require route-specific capabilities: storage configuration and destination changes should require `backwpup_jobs_edit` and/or `backwpup_settings`, while backup execution should require `backwpup_jobs_start`. Mirror those checks inside the mutation methods so UI-only gating cannot be bypassed through REST.",
    "patchstack_eligible": false,
    "sink_snippet": "  546                  $create_args['Key'] = $job_object->job['s3dir'] . $job_object->backup_file;\n  547                  $create_args['ContentType'] = MimeTypeExtractor::fromFilePath($job_object->backup_folder . $job_object->backup_file);\n  548                  $create_args['ContentMD5'] = base64_encode(md5_file($job_object->backup_folder . $job_object->backup_file, true));\n  549  \n  550                  try {\n  551                      $s3->putObject($create_args);\n  552                  } catch (Exception $e) {\n  553                      $errorMessage = $e->getMessage();\n  554                      if ($e instanceof AwsException) {\n  555                          $errorMessage = $e->getAwsErrorMessage();\n  556                      }\n",
    "source_snippet": "  257  \t *\n  258  \t * @param WP_REST_Request $request\n  259  \t * @throws Exception If the cloud name is not set or the cloud is not found.\n  260  \t * @return \\WP_REST_Response The response object containing the HTML content and status.\n  261  \t */\n  262  \tpublic function cloud_save_and_test( WP_REST_Request $request ) {\n  263  \t\t$params = $request->get_params();\n  264  \n  265  \t\t$return = [];\n  266  \t\t$status = 200;\n  267  \t\ttry {\n"
  }
}
