  "phase2_finding": {
    "finding_id": "BWPUP-P2-002",
    "verdict": "TP",
    "vuln_type": "Broken Access Control",
    "cwe_id": "CWE-862",
    "severity": "medium",
    "auth_required": "plugin-defined read-only role backwpup_check",
    "confidence": "high",
    "entry_point_id": "ep_rest_backwpup_v1__process_bulk_actions",
    "source_function": "WPMedia\\BackWPup\\Backups\\API\\Rest::process_bulk_actions",
    "sink_function": "BackWPup_Destination_Folder::file_delete",
    "source_file_path": "src/Backups/API/Rest.php",
    "source_line_number": 360,
    "sink_file_path": "inc/class-destination-folder.php",
    "sink_line_number": 75,
    "file_path": "inc/class-destination-folder.php",
    "line_number": 75,
    "reasoning": {
      "hypothesis": "A `backwpup_check` user can delete stored backup archives through the REST bulk-action endpoint even though the role intentionally lacks `backwpup_backups_delete`.",
      "trace": [
        "`backwpup_check` is created with `backwpup_backups=true` but `backwpup_backups_delete=false` in `inc/class-install.php:143-157`.",
        "The REST bulk-delete route `/process_bulk_actions` is exposed with `permission_callback => [ $this, 'has_permission' ]` in `src/Backups/API/Rest.php:122-128`, and `has_permission()` only checks `current_user_can('backwpup')` in `src/Backups/API/Rest.php:81-82`.",
        "`process_bulk_actions()` calls `delete_backup()` for each supplied item in `src/Backups/API/Rest.php:360-385`.",
        "`delete_backup()` resolves the destination from the attacker-supplied `data-url` payload and dispatches to `$dest_class->file_delete( $jobdest, $file )` in `src/Backups/API/Rest.php:395-410`.",
        "For the default local-folder destination, `BackWPup_Destination_Folder::file_delete()` resolves the selected archive under the configured backup directory and deletes it with `wp_delete_file()` in `inc/class-destination-folder.php:62-75`."
      ],
      "defenses": [
        "The legacy Backups UI uses the stricter capability consistently: delete buttons are only rendered for `backwpup_backups_delete` in `inc/class-page-backups.php:390-391`, and the legacy delete action dies if that capability is missing in `inc/class-page-backups.php:503-540`."
      ],
      "refutation": [
        {
          "attempt": "Check whether the role mismatch is only cosmetic in the UI and the backend ultimately enforces `backwpup_backups_delete`.",
          "result": "not_refuted",
          "details": "The REST backend never checks `backwpup_backups_delete`; it only requires `backwpup` before calling `file_delete()`."
        },
        {
          "attempt": "Check whether the sink is actually an arbitrary-file-delete primitive rather than a backup-only delete path.",
          "result": "refuted_as_different_issue",
          "details": "`inc/class-destination-folder.php:69-75` constrains deletion to `basename()` under the configured backup directory and requires a real file. The confirmed issue is authorization bypass for backup deletion, not path traversal."
        }
      ],
      "conclusion": "This is a confirmed authorization bypass for destructive backup actions. The shipped read-only role can delete existing backup archives through REST even though both the role definition and the legacy controller treat backup deletion as a separate privileged action."
    },
    "poc_description": "Assign `backwpup_check` to a test user, log in, load a BackWPup page to obtain `backwpupApi.nonce`, then POST to `/wp-json/backwpup/v1/process_bulk_actions` with `action=delete` and a `backups[0][dataset][data-url]` value copied from a backup row. The selected local backup archive is deleted although the role lacks `backwpup_backups_delete`.",
    "cvss_vector": "AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
    "remediation": "Require `backwpup_backups_delete` for destructive backup routes, both in the REST route registration and inside the delete handler. Do not reuse the general `backwpup` capability for state-changing operations.",
    "patchstack_eligible": false,
    "sink_snippet": "   70  \t\t$backup_dir = BackWPup_File::get_absolute_path( $backup_dir );\n   71  \n   72  \t\t$backupfile = realpath( trailingslashit( $backup_dir ) . basename( $backupfile ) );\n   73  \n   74  \t\tif ( $backupfile && is_writable( $backupfile ) && ! is_dir( $backupfile ) && ! is_link( $backupfile ) ) { //phpcs:ignore\n   75  \t\t\twp_delete_file( $backupfile );\n   76  \t\t} else {\n   77  \t\t\t// translators: %s: backup file path.\n   78  \t\t\t\\BackWPup_Admin::message( sprintf( __( 'Could not delete backup archive \"%s\", check permissions!', 'backwpup' ), $backupfile ), true );\n   79  \t\t}\n   80  \t}\n",
    "source_snippet": "  355  \t *\n  356  \t * @return WP_REST_Response The response object containing the status and message.\n  357  \t *\n  358  \t * @throws Exception If an error occurs during the process.\n  359  \t */\n  360  \tpublic function process_bulk_actions( WP_REST_Request $request ): \\WP_REST_Response {\n  361  \t\t$params   = $request->get_params();\n  362  \t\t$response = [\n  363  \t\t\t'success' => [],\n  364  \t\t\t'errors'  => [],\n  365  \t\t];\n"
